+````markdown name=ops/docs/run_and_interpretation.md
+# Run, interpret and act — Production Proofs (step‑by‑step)
+
+This document describes exact runnable commands, what outputs to look for, how to interpret failures, and how to create remediation tickets and track progress.
+
+Prerequisites
+- kubectl configured to target the cluster with Tekton installed.
+- AWS CLI configured (or IRSA) with write access to the evidence S3 bucket.
+- gh CLI authenticated for issue creation (optional).
+- cosign keys available for signing (or use an HSM/KMS signer).
+
+Quick run options (pick one)
+1) In‑cluster Tekton PipelineRun (preferred)
+   - Ensure the YAML is prefilled: `ops/tekton/pipelineruns/production_proofs_pr_prefilled.yaml`
+   - Apply:
+     - chmod +x ops/tekton/apply_prefilled_pr.sh
+     - ./ops/tekton/apply_prefilled_pr.sh
+   - Monitor:
+     - kubectl -n cicd get pipelineruns -w
+     - kubectl -n cicd get tasks -o wide
+     - kubectl -n cicd logs <task-pod> -c step-name
+
+2) Dispatch via GitHub Actions (remote)
+   - Either use gh:
+     - ./ops/ci/dispatch_run.sh   # uses gh if available
+   - Or run with API (curl) — script will use curl fallback if gh missing (requires GITHUB_TOKEN)
+
+What to expect in S3 (evidence bucket)
+- production_proofs/summary-<ts>.json — orchestrator summary
+- hpo/submissions/manifest-*.json — HPO submission metadata
+- checkpoints/*.json — per-trial checkpoint artifacts
+- longshadow/*.json and longshadow/postmortem-*.json
+- stress/2k-*.json
+- otel/coverage-*.json and trace→evidence manifests under otel/ or traces/
+- opa/verdict-*.json and opa/harness-report/*
+- remediation/metrics/*.json and remediation/verdict-*.json
+- compliance/audit-*.json and bundled evidence under evidence-bundles/
+
+Validator commands (post-run)
+- Checkpoint analysis:
+  python3 services/hpo/checkpoint_analyzer.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod --threshold 0.90
+  - Output: {"total_trials": X, "successful": Y, "success_rate": 0.93}
+  - Pass condition: success_rate >= threshold.
+
+- OTEL coverage:
+  python3 services/telemetry/otel_span_coverage_checker.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+  - Output: {"ts": "...", "coverage": 0.93, "s3_key":"..."}
+  - Pass condition: coverage >= OTEL_THRESHOLD (0.90)
+
+- OPA harness verdict:
+  python3 services/decisioning/opa_full_harness_runner.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+  - Produces opa/verdict-*.json with mismatch_rate.
+  - Pass condition: mismatch_rate <= 0.01 (adjust to policy risk tolerance)
+
+- Remediation analyzer:
+  python3 services/failure/remediation_analyzer.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod --threshold 0.90
+  - Reads remediation/metrics and fails non-zero exit code if below threshold.
+
+- Explainability attachment verification:
+  python3 services/explainability/manifest_index_and_attach.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+  - Verifies manifest presence, ACLs and attaches manifest to promotion evidence.
+
+- Long-term SLO and audit:
+  python3 services/reliability/longterm_slo_collector_signer.py --evidence s3://aegis-evidence-prod
+  - Produces weekly/monthly reports and (if key available) cosign signatures.
+
+How to interpret common failure modes
+- Checkpoint success < threshold:
+  - Look at S3 checkpoints/*.json for patterns: missing checkpoint files, corrupted upload or failed trials.
+  - Typical root causes: resource constraints, Ray job failures, data driver errors.
+  - Actions: increase resources, fix driver errors, resubmit HPO partials.
+
+- OTEL coverage low:
+  - Inspect otel/coverage-*.json for span categories missing.
+  - Check instrumentation in model-serving and validation tasks for run_id and business_kpi annotations.
+
+- OPA mismatch rate high:
+  - Download opa/harness-report/* and inspect mismatches.
+  - Determine whether policy needs tuning or model behavior is risky; create mitigation ticket.
+
+- Remediation success low:
+  - Inspect remediation/metrics/* for types of incidents that didn't auto-resolve.
+  - Add remediation playbooks or tuning, expand remediation_engine runbooks/permissions.
+
+- Pen-test critical findings:
+  - Stop promotion. Create security tickets, remediate with priority, then re-run ops/security/pen_test_retest_and_verify.sh.
+
+Generate remediation backlog & issues
+- Generate markdown backlog:
+  python3 ops/scripts/generate_remediation_tickets.py --input /tmp/acceptance.json --out /tmp/remediation_backlog.md
+- Create issues (requires gh auth):
+  python3 ops/scripts/generate_remediation_tickets.py --input /tmp/acceptance.json --out /tmp/remediation_backlog.md --create-issues --repo rsinghunjan/aegis --assignee rsinghunjan
+- Or use the wrapper:
+  chmod +x ops/scripts/create_remediation_issues.sh
+  ./ops/scripts/create_remediation_issues.sh --input /tmp/acceptance.json
+
+Regression & re-run plan (fast iterations)
+1. Fix highest impact items from backlog: HPO checkpoint drivers, OTEL instrumentation, OPA rule tuning, remediation playbooks, security fixes.
+2. Re-run only impacted validators:
+   - For OTEL: run services/telemetry/otel_span_coverage_checker.py
+   - For OPA: run services/decisioning/opa_full_harness_runner.py
+   - For remediation: run services/failure/remediation_validation.py
+3. Re-run the full pipeline once critical items pass to produce fresh evidence.
+
+What I will watch for when you run
+- A checkpoint success_rate >= 0.90 across trials.
+- OTEL coverage >= 0.90 for critical spans with run_id & business_kpi.
+- OPA mismatch rate <= 0.01 on harness.
+- Remediation success >= 0.90 and no blocking critical pen-test findings.
+- Evidence bundles cosign-signed and audit reports uploaded & verifiable.
+
+If you want, I can:
+- Prefill and commit any additional manifests (e.g., different bucket, different trial count).
+- Generate a prioritized sprint backlog from a real acceptance.json you upload.
+- Walk through the first run in a live session and interpret logs with you.
+
+````
